<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<mtmd:ModelingTaskMetaData xmlns:stc="http://ssp-standard.org/SSPTraceability1/SSPTraceabilityCommon" xmlns:mtmd="http://ssp-standard.org/SSPTraceability1/ModelingTaskMetaData" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:ssc="http://ssp-standard.org/SSP1/SystemStructureCommon" version="1.0.0" name="TorqueControl Modelling Task" GUID="d5d1ebcb-a97b-46ff-8ffe-31b133975c18" generationTool="LOTAR 2026 worked example (Claude)" generationDateAndTime="2026-08-07T00:00:00Z">
  <mtmd:GeneralInformation><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_gi1"><stc:Content>Modelling task record for EVExample.FMUs.TorqueArbitration (torque-arbitration / regenerative-braking blending controller). Extended for this task with a new 'AgressiveRegeneration' parameter variant implementing more aggressive regen-torque blending, per AutoSARTorqueArbitrationReq.md.</stc:Content></stc:Resource><stc:ResourceReference xlink:href="DecisionTask.dtmd" xlink:type="simple"/><stc:Classification type="org.credible-process.core"><stc:ClassificationEntry keyword="model-validation.mode">internal</stc:ClassificationEntry></stc:Classification></mtmd:GeneralInformation>
  <mtmd:AnalysisPhase>
    <mtmd:AnalyzeModelingTaskAndObjectives><stc:Input><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_an_in"><stc:Content>DecisionTask.dtmd DefineSubTasks output and SimulationTask.stmd ImplementModel step, scoping EVExample.FMUs.TorqueArbitration as a sub-task of the range-substantiation simulation task.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Input><stc:Procedure><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_an_proc"><stc:Content>Reviewed EVExample.FMUs.TorqueArbitration's role in the overall task against ControllerAndModelInterfaces.md and the SRMD's stated question of interest.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Procedure><stc:Output><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_an_out"><stc:Content>Modelling objective: defining the new AgressiveRegeneration blending behaviour and the AUTOSAR-derived interface constraints it must respect.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Output><stc:Rationale><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_an_rat"><stc:Content>Extended for this task with a new 'AgressiveRegeneration' parameter variant implementing more aggressive regen-torque blending, per AutoSARTorqueArbitrationReq.md.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Rationale><stc:LifeCycleInformation><stc:Approved date="2026-06-20T09:00:00Z"><stc:Responsible organization="MBI LLC - Vehicle Energy Systems CAE" role="Simulation Engineer" name="T. Okafor"/><ssc:Signature role="authenticity" type="application/xml"/></stc:Approved></stc:LifeCycleInformation></mtmd:AnalyzeModelingTaskAndObjectives>
    <mtmd:VerifyAnalysis><stc:Input><stc:ResourceReference xlink:href="#id_tc_an_out"/></stc:Input><stc:Procedure><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_va_proc"><stc:Content>Independent read-through of the modelling objective against the spawning STMD's ImplementModel step.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Procedure><stc:Output><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_va_out"><stc:Content>Sign-off memo: modelling objective is traceable and consistent with the task-level requirement.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Output><stc:Rationale><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_va_rat"><stc:Content>Independent check before Requirements work begins.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Rationale><stc:LifeCycleInformation><stc:Approved date="2026-06-20T11:00:00Z"><stc:Responsible organization="MBI LLC - Vehicle Energy Systems CAE" role="Verification and Validation Engineer" name="P. Lindqvist"/><ssc:Signature role="authenticity" type="application/xml"/></stc:Approved></stc:LifeCycleInformation></mtmd:VerifyAnalysis>
  </mtmd:AnalysisPhase>
  <mtmd:RequirementsPhase>
    <mtmd:DefineModelRequirements><stc:Input><stc:ResourceReference xlink:href="#id_tc_an_out"/></stc:Input><stc:Procedure><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_dmr_proc"><stc:Content>Derived from defining the new AgressiveRegeneration blending behaviour and the AUTOSAR-derived interface constraints it must respect.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Procedure><stc:Output><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_dmr_out"><stc:Content>Model requirements: brake/accelerator command inputs (brk_cmd, acc_cmd) and vehicle-velocity input (veh_vel_x) must map to tau_brake_ref / tau_ref_rear[1] outputs per the existing torque-arbitration interface; the new AgressiveRegeneration variant must increase regenerative-torque utilisation without exceeding tauBrakeMax or violating the AUTOSAR torque-arbitration constraints in AutoSARTorqueArbitrationReq.md.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Output><stc:Rationale><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_dmr_rat"><stc:Content>Directly derived from AutoSARTorqueArbitrationReq.md and ControllerRequirements.md, already present in this archive's extra/ folder.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Rationale><stc:LifeCycleInformation><stc:Approved date="2026-06-20T13:00:00Z"><stc:Responsible organization="MBI LLC - Vehicle Energy Systems CAE" role="Simulation Engineer" name="T. Okafor"/><ssc:Signature role="authenticity" type="application/xml"/></stc:Approved></stc:LifeCycleInformation></mtmd:DefineModelRequirements>
    <mtmd:DefineParameterRequirements><stc:Input><stc:ResourceReference xlink:href="#id_tc_dmr_out"/></stc:Input><stc:Procedure><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_dpr_proc"><stc:Content>Identified parameters needing documented uncertainty/variant bounds.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Procedure><stc:Output><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_dpr_out"><stc:Content>Parameter requirements: v_min, v_max, throttle_min, regen_torque, tauMax, tauBrakeMax, drive_proportion, enable_regen_braking -- the AgressiveRegeneration variant must lower v_min/v_max thresholds and reduce tauBrakeMax relative to baseline to shift more braking torque onto the e-machine.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Output><stc:Rationale><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_dpr_rat"><stc:Content>Matches the parameter set already exercised by the spawning STMD's DefineParameterRequirements step.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Rationale><stc:LifeCycleInformation><stc:Approved date="2026-06-20T14:00:00Z"><stc:Responsible organization="MBI LLC - Vehicle Energy Systems CAE" role="Simulation Engineer" name="T. Okafor"/><ssc:Signature role="authenticity" type="application/xml"/></stc:Approved></stc:LifeCycleInformation></mtmd:DefineParameterRequirements>
    <mtmd:DefineSimulationEnvironmentRequirements><stc:Input><stc:ResourceReference xlink:href="#id_tc_dmr_out"/></stc:Input><stc:Procedure><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_dser_proc"><stc:Content>Derived from the company code-verification standard.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Procedure><stc:Output><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_dser_out"><stc:Content>FMI 2.0 Co-Simulation, Optimica Compiler Toolkit, adaptive solver tolerance &lt;=1e-6, matching the packaged modelDescription.xml.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Output><stc:Rationale><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_dser_rat"><stc:Content>Consistent with the task-level environment requirement.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Rationale><stc:LifeCycleInformation><stc:Approved date="2026-06-20T15:00:00Z"><stc:Responsible organization="MBI LLC - Vehicle Energy Systems CAE" role="Simulation Engineer" name="T. Okafor"/><ssc:Signature role="authenticity" type="application/xml"/></stc:Approved></stc:LifeCycleInformation></mtmd:DefineSimulationEnvironmentRequirements>
    <mtmd:DefineSimulationIntegrationRequirements><stc:Input><stc:ResourceReference xlink:href="#id_tc_dmr_out"/></stc:Input><stc:Procedure><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_dsir_proc"><stc:Content>Reviewed the model's causal signal interface against ControllerAndModelInterfaces.md.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Procedure><stc:Output><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_dsir_out"><stc:Content>Integration requirements: nested inside the 'Controllers' subsystem alongside DriverCycleType, consuming its brk_cmd/acc_cmd outputs and the top-level speed_m signal.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Output><stc:Rationale><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_dsir_rat"><stc:Content>Matches the interface already wired in SystemStructure.ssd.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Rationale><stc:LifeCycleInformation><stc:Approved date="2026-06-20T16:00:00Z"><stc:Responsible organization="MBI LLC - Vehicle Energy Systems CAE" role="Simulation Engineer" name="T. Okafor"/><ssc:Signature role="authenticity" type="application/xml"/></stc:Approved></stc:LifeCycleInformation></mtmd:DefineSimulationIntegrationRequirements>
    <mtmd:DefineTestCaseRequirements><stc:Input><stc:ResourceReference xlink:href="#id_tc_dmr_out"/></stc:Input><stc:Procedure><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_dtcr_proc"><stc:Content>Derived acceptance criteria for this model from the task-level test cases it participates in.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Procedure><stc:Output><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_dtcr_out"><stc:Content>Test-case requirements: must be exercised under both baseline and AgressiveRegeneration parameterisation in the task-level test cases (simulation1 vs. simulation2).</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Output><stc:Rationale><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_dtcr_rat"><stc:Content>Model-level test criteria are a refinement of, not a replacement for, the task-level test cases defined in SimulationTask.stmd.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Rationale><stc:LifeCycleInformation><stc:Approved date="2026-06-20T17:00:00Z"><stc:Responsible organization="MBI LLC - Vehicle Energy Systems CAE" role="Simulation Engineer" name="T. Okafor"/><ssc:Signature role="authenticity" type="application/xml"/></stc:Approved></stc:LifeCycleInformation></mtmd:DefineTestCaseRequirements>
    <mtmd:DefineQualityAssuranceRequirements><stc:Input><stc:ResourceReference xlink:href="#id_tc_dtcr_out"/></stc:Input><stc:Procedure><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_dqar_proc"><stc:Content>Applied the task-level QA plan at model granularity.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Procedure><stc:Output><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_dqar_out"><stc:Content>QA plan: independent verification review at end of Requirements and Design; independent setup/results review before integration.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Output><stc:Rationale><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_dqar_rat"><stc:Content>Mirrors SimulationTask.stmd's DefineQualityAssuranceRequirements, scoped to this model.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Rationale><stc:LifeCycleInformation><stc:Approved date="2026-06-20T18:00:00Z"><stc:Responsible organization="MBI LLC - Vehicle Energy Systems CAE" role="Verification and Validation Engineer" name="P. Lindqvist"/><ssc:Signature role="authenticity" type="application/xml"/></stc:Approved></stc:LifeCycleInformation></mtmd:DefineQualityAssuranceRequirements>
    <mtmd:VerifyRequirements><stc:Input><stc:ResourceReference xlink:href="#id_tc_dmr_out"/><stc:ResourceReference xlink:href="#id_tc_dpr_out"/><stc:ResourceReference xlink:href="#id_tc_dser_out"/><stc:ResourceReference xlink:href="#id_tc_dsir_out"/><stc:ResourceReference xlink:href="#id_tc_dtcr_out"/><stc:ResourceReference xlink:href="#id_tc_dqar_out"/></stc:Input><stc:Procedure><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_vr_proc"><stc:Content>Independent QA cross-check of all model-level Requirements outputs.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Procedure><stc:Output><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_vr_out"><stc:Content>Requirements sign-off memo: no open issues.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Output><stc:Rationale><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_vr_rat"><stc:Content>Gates entry into Design.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Rationale><stc:LifeCycleInformation><stc:Approved date="2026-06-21T09:00:00Z"><stc:Responsible organization="MBI LLC - Vehicle Energy Systems CAE" role="Verification and Validation Engineer" name="P. Lindqvist"/><ssc:Signature role="authenticity" type="application/xml"/></stc:Approved></stc:LifeCycleInformation></mtmd:VerifyRequirements>
  </mtmd:RequirementsPhase>
  <mtmd:DesignPhase>
    <mtmd:DefineModelDesignSpecification><stc:Input><stc:ResourceReference xlink:href="#id_tc_dmr_out"/></stc:Input><stc:Procedure><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_dmds_proc"><stc:Content>Defined the AgressiveRegeneration parameter set as a delta against the baseline blending strategy, keeping the control logic (FMU binary) unchanged and expressing the behaviour change entirely through parameters.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Procedure><stc:Output><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_dmds_out"><stc:Content>Design decision: AgressiveRegeneration variant lowers v_min from 2.0 to 0.5 m/s and v_max is held at 27.777 m/s, reduces tauBrakeMax toward 0 N.m (shifting nearly all braking torque to regen within tauMax=1000 N.m), matching the values already present in SystemStructure.ssd's easySSP:ParameterContainer for this variant.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Output><stc:Rationale><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_dmds_rat"><stc:Content>A parameter-only change (no new control logic) keeps the change auditable against AutoSARTorqueArbitrationReq.md and avoids the higher-risk step of modifying verified control code.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Rationale><stc:LifeCycleInformation><stc:Approved date="2026-06-23T09:00:00Z"><stc:Responsible organization="MBI LLC - Vehicle Energy Systems CAE" role="Simulation Engineer" name="T. Okafor"/><ssc:Signature role="authenticity" type="application/xml"/></stc:Approved></stc:LifeCycleInformation></mtmd:DefineModelDesignSpecification>
    <mtmd:DefineParameterDesignSpecification><stc:Input><stc:ResourceReference xlink:href="#id_tc_dpr_out"/></stc:Input><stc:Procedure><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_dpds_proc"><stc:Content>Mapped parameter requirements onto the ssv:ParameterSet / easySSP:ParameterContainer mechanism.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Procedure><stc:Output><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_dpds_out"><stc:Content>Parameter design: AgressiveRegeneration variant values as specified in DefineModelDesignSpecification's Output, expressed as an easySSP:ParameterContainer sibling to the existing 1_ExtendedRange/2_ExtendedPlusRange/3_HighPowerExtendedRange variants.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Output><stc:Rationale><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_dpds_rat"><stc:Content>Reuses the existing variant-container pattern.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Rationale><stc:LifeCycleInformation><stc:Approved date="2026-06-23T11:00:00Z"><stc:Responsible organization="MBI LLC - Vehicle Energy Systems CAE" role="Simulation Engineer" name="T. Okafor"/><ssc:Signature role="authenticity" type="application/xml"/></stc:Approved></stc:LifeCycleInformation></mtmd:DefineParameterDesignSpecification>
    <mtmd:DefineSimulationEnvironmentDesignSpecification><stc:Input><stc:ResourceReference xlink:href="#id_tc_dser_out"/></stc:Input><stc:Procedure><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_dsends_proc"><stc:Content>Pinned the exact tool/solver combination recorded in the packaged modelDescription.xml.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Procedure><stc:Output><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_dsends_out"><stc:Content>Optimica Compiler Toolkit, CVode-class adaptive solver, tolerance 1e-6.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Output><stc:Rationale><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_dsends_rat"><stc:Content>Required for archival re-executability.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Rationale><stc:LifeCycleInformation><stc:Approved date="2026-06-24T09:00:00Z"><stc:Responsible organization="MBI LLC - Vehicle Energy Systems CAE" role="Simulation Engineer" name="T. Okafor"/><ssc:Signature role="authenticity" type="application/xml"/></stc:Approved></stc:LifeCycleInformation></mtmd:DefineSimulationEnvironmentDesignSpecification>
    <mtmd:DefineSimulationIntegrationDesignSpecification><stc:Input><stc:ResourceReference xlink:href="#id_tc_dsir_out"/></stc:Input><stc:Procedure><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_dsids_proc"><stc:Content>Confirmed the model's connector wiring against SystemStructure.ssd.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Procedure><stc:Output><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_dsids_out"><stc:Content>Integration design: TorqueArbitration Component's brk_cmd/acc_cmd inputs wired from DriverCycleType, veh_vel_x wired from the Controllers subsystem's speed_m input, tau_brake_ref/tau_ref_rear[1] outputs wired to the subsystem boundary -- exactly as implemented in SystemStructure.ssd.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Output><stc:Rationale><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_dsids_rat"><stc:Content>Confirms the existing wiring satisfies the requirement.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Rationale><stc:LifeCycleInformation><stc:Approved date="2026-06-24T11:00:00Z"><stc:Responsible organization="MBI LLC - Vehicle Energy Systems CAE" role="Simulation Engineer" name="T. Okafor"/><ssc:Signature role="authenticity" type="application/xml"/></stc:Approved></stc:LifeCycleInformation></mtmd:DefineSimulationIntegrationDesignSpecification>
    <mtmd:DefineTestCaseDesignSpecification><stc:Input><stc:ResourceReference xlink:href="#id_tc_dtcr_out"/></stc:Input><stc:Procedure><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_dtcds_proc"><stc:Content>Mapped model-level test criteria onto the task-level run folders.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Procedure><stc:Output><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_dtcds_out"><stc:Content>Test-case design: simulation1 exercises the baseline parameter set, simulation2 exercises AgressiveRegeneration -- the direct comparison this task's primary KPI (range gain from more aggressive blending) depends on.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Output><stc:Rationale><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_dtcds_rat"><stc:Content>Consistent with SimulationTask.stmd's DefineTestCaseDesignSpecification.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Rationale><stc:LifeCycleInformation><stc:Approved date="2026-06-25T09:00:00Z"><stc:Responsible organization="MBI LLC - Vehicle Energy Systems CAE" role="Simulation Engineer" name="T. Okafor"/><ssc:Signature role="authenticity" type="application/xml"/></stc:Approved></stc:LifeCycleInformation></mtmd:DefineTestCaseDesignSpecification>
    <mtmd:DefineQualityAssuranceDesignSpecification><stc:Input><stc:ResourceReference xlink:href="#id_tc_dqar_out"/></stc:Input><stc:Procedure><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_dqads_proc"><stc:Content>Turned the model-level QA plan into concrete criteria.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Procedure><stc:Output><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_dqads_out"><stc:Content>Checklist: modelDescription.xml declares fmiVersion 2.0 and CoSimulation; connector units match; parameter defaults documented.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Output><stc:Rationale><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_dqads_rat"><stc:Content>Model-specific refinement of the task-level QA checklist.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Rationale><stc:LifeCycleInformation><stc:Approved date="2026-06-25T11:00:00Z"><stc:Responsible organization="MBI LLC - Vehicle Energy Systems CAE" role="Verification and Validation Engineer" name="P. Lindqvist"/><ssc:Signature role="authenticity" type="application/xml"/></stc:Approved></stc:LifeCycleInformation></mtmd:DefineQualityAssuranceDesignSpecification>
    <mtmd:VerifyDesignSpecification><stc:Input><stc:ResourceReference xlink:href="#id_tc_dmds_out"/><stc:ResourceReference xlink:href="#id_tc_dpds_out"/><stc:ResourceReference xlink:href="#id_tc_dsends_out"/><stc:ResourceReference xlink:href="#id_tc_dsids_out"/><stc:ResourceReference xlink:href="#id_tc_dtcds_out"/><stc:ResourceReference xlink:href="#id_tc_dqads_out"/></stc:Input><stc:Procedure><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_vds_proc"><stc:Content>Independent design review.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Procedure><stc:Output><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_vds_out"><stc:Content>Design sign-off memo: no open issues.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Output><stc:Rationale><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_vds_rat"><stc:Content>Gates entry into Implementation.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Rationale><stc:LifeCycleInformation><stc:Approved date="2026-06-26T09:00:00Z"><stc:Responsible organization="MBI LLC - Vehicle Energy Systems CAE" role="Verification and Validation Engineer" name="P. Lindqvist"/><ssc:Signature role="authenticity" type="application/xml"/></stc:Approved></stc:LifeCycleInformation></mtmd:VerifyDesignSpecification>
  </mtmd:DesignPhase>
  <mtmd:ImplementationPhase>
    <mtmd:ImplementModel><stc:Input><stc:ResourceReference xlink:href="#id_tc_dmds_out"/></stc:Input><stc:Procedure><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_im_proc"><stc:Content>Implemented the AgressiveRegeneration parameter variant and verified its torque outputs stay within tauMax/tauBrakeMax bounds across the WLTP cycle before handing off to task-level integration.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Procedure><stc:Output><stc:Resource kind="model" type="application/x-fmu-sharedlibrary" id="id_tc_im_out"><stc:Content>Packaged Optimica Compiler Toolkit-compiled FMI 2.0 CoSimulation FMU, resources/TorqueControl.fmu (archive top-level resources/ directory; not referenced by relative path here since it sits outside this MTMD's own extra/org.ssp-standard.ssp-traceability.mtmd/ folder).</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Output><stc:Rationale><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_im_rat"><stc:Content>Bounding torque outputs before integration catches a mis-parameterised variant at the model level, where it is cheap to fix, rather than at task-level execution.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Rationale><stc:LifeCycleInformation><stc:Approved date="2026-07-01T09:00:00Z"><stc:Responsible organization="MBI LLC - Vehicle Energy Systems CAE" role="Simulation Engineer" name="T. Okafor"/><ssc:Signature role="authenticity" type="application/xml"/></stc:Approved></stc:LifeCycleInformation></mtmd:ImplementModel>
    <mtmd:ImplementParameter><stc:Input><stc:ResourceReference xlink:href="#id_tc_dpds_out"/></stc:Input><stc:Procedure><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_ip_proc"><stc:Content>Committed the designed parameter sets into the packaged SSD/SSV files.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Procedure><stc:Output><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_ip_out"><stc:Content>Confirmed: the AgressiveRegeneration easySSP:ParameterContainer is present and populated in both SystemStructure.ssd and EVRangeExampleNEDC.ssd.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Output><stc:Rationale><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_ip_rat"><stc:Content>Keeps the archived package self-contained.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Rationale><stc:LifeCycleInformation><stc:Approved date="2026-07-01T11:00:00Z"><stc:Responsible organization="MBI LLC - Vehicle Energy Systems CAE" role="Simulation Engineer" name="T. Okafor"/><ssc:Signature role="authenticity" type="application/xml"/></stc:Approved></stc:LifeCycleInformation></mtmd:ImplementParameter>
    <mtmd:ImplementSimulationEnvironment><stc:Input><stc:ResourceReference xlink:href="#id_tc_dsends_out"/></stc:Input><stc:Procedure><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_ise_proc"><stc:Content>Confirmed the packaged FMU matches the pinned environment design.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Procedure><stc:Output><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_ise_out"><stc:Content>Confirmed: TorqueControl.fmu, generationTool="Optimica Compiler Toolkit", FMI 2.0 CoSimulation.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Output><stc:Rationale><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_ise_rat"><stc:Content>Required for MTMD's own archival re-executability.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Rationale><stc:LifeCycleInformation><stc:Approved date="2026-07-01T13:00:00Z"><stc:Responsible organization="MBI LLC - Vehicle Energy Systems CAE" role="Simulation Engineer" name="T. Okafor"/><ssc:Signature role="authenticity" type="application/xml"/></stc:Approved></stc:LifeCycleInformation></mtmd:ImplementSimulationEnvironment>
    <mtmd:ImplementTestCase><stc:Input><stc:ResourceReference xlink:href="#id_tc_dtcds_out"/></stc:Input><stc:Procedure><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_itc_proc"><stc:Content>Confirmed the model-level test criteria are exercised by the shared task-level config.json run definitions.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Procedure><stc:Output><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_itc_out"><stc:Content>No model-specific test harness needed beyond the shared task-level runs; criteria satisfied by simulation1/2/3.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Output><stc:Rationale><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_itc_rat"><stc:Content>Avoids duplicating test infrastructure already implemented at task level.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Rationale><stc:LifeCycleInformation><stc:Approved date="2026-07-01T15:00:00Z"><stc:Responsible organization="MBI LLC - Vehicle Energy Systems CAE" role="Simulation Engineer" name="T. Okafor"/><ssc:Signature role="authenticity" type="application/xml"/></stc:Approved></stc:LifeCycleInformation></mtmd:ImplementTestCase>
    <mtmd:IntegrateSimulation><stc:Input><stc:ResourceReference xlink:href="#id_tc_dsids_out"/></stc:Input><stc:Procedure><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_is_proc"><stc:Content>Confirmed the model's connectors resolve correctly inside SystemStructure.ssd's ssd:Connections.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Procedure><stc:Output><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_is_out"><stc:Content>Confirmed: all connectors used by this model are wired and unit-consistent in the integrated SSD.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Output><stc:Rationale><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_is_rat"><stc:Content>Model-level confirmation of the task-level integration work.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Rationale><stc:LifeCycleInformation><stc:Approved date="2026-07-02T09:00:00Z"><stc:Responsible organization="MBI LLC - Vehicle Energy Systems CAE" role="Simulation Engineer" name="T. Okafor"/><ssc:Signature role="authenticity" type="application/xml"/></stc:Approved></stc:LifeCycleInformation></mtmd:IntegrateSimulation>
    <mtmd:AssureSimulationSetupQuality><stc:Input><stc:ResourceReference xlink:href="#id_tc_is_out"/></stc:Input><stc:Procedure><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_assq_proc"><stc:Content>Ran the model-level QA checklist.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Procedure><stc:Output><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_assq_out"><stc:Content>Setup QA memo: 0 defects found for this model's contribution to the integrated setup.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Output><stc:Rationale><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_assq_rat"><stc:Content>Clean setup QA supports proceeding to task-level execution.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Rationale><stc:LifeCycleInformation><stc:Approved date="2026-07-02T11:00:00Z"><stc:Responsible organization="MBI LLC - Vehicle Energy Systems CAE" role="Verification and Validation Engineer" name="P. Lindqvist"/><ssc:Signature role="authenticity" type="application/xml"/></stc:Approved></stc:LifeCycleInformation></mtmd:AssureSimulationSetupQuality>
    <mtmd:DeriveSimulationSetupQualityVerdict><stc:Input><stc:ResourceReference xlink:href="#id_tc_assq_out"/></stc:Input><stc:Procedure><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_dssqv_proc"><stc:Content>QA reviewer verdict for this model.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Procedure><stc:Output><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_dssqv_out"><stc:Content>Verdict: model setup APPROVED.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Output><stc:Rationale><stc:Resource kind="document" type="text/markdown" id="id_tc_dssqv_rat"><stc:Content>0 defects supports unconditional approval.</stc:Content></stc:Resource></stc:Rationale><stc:LifeCycleInformation><stc:Approved date="2026-07-02T13:00:00Z"><stc:Responsible organization="MBI LLC - Vehicle Energy Systems CAE" role="Verification and Validation Engineer" name="P. Lindqvist"/><ssc:Signature role="authenticity" type="application/xml"/></stc:Approved></stc:LifeCycleInformation></mtmd:DeriveSimulationSetupQualityVerdict>
